@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho

node "Operator device" as Device {
  artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Docker Compose / Linux host" as Host {
  node "web service/container" as Web {
    artifact "React static UI\n(+ reverse proxy in remote demo)" as React
  }
  node "api service/container" as Api {
    artifact "Spring Boot modular monolith" as Spring
    artifact "StaticPolicyAdapter /\nDeterministicAnalysisStub" as Offline
  }
  database "db service/container\nPostgreSQL + pgvector" as DB
}

cloud "Optional external AI provider" as Provider

Browser --> Web : HTTP localhost\nor HTTPS remote demo
Web --> Api : HTTP/JSON /api/*\nCompose/private network
Api --> DB : JDBC / PostgreSQL protocol\nTCP 5432 private network
Api ..> Provider : HTTPS provider API\nonly when explicitly configured
Api --> Offline : in-process baseline path

note bottom of Host
  Baseline communication is synchronous request/response.
  No WebSocket, event broker, FIFO, Redis or separate identity service is
  assumed. Those would require an actual design/implementation need.
  The database port is not exposed publicly.
end note
@enduml
